# Bottom Navbar Pattern

## Overview
DECM uses a flexible bottom navigation bar system that combines Context API, Zustand state management, and variant-based component composition for feature-specific navigation components.

## Component Location
`apps/web/src/components/BottomContainer/`

## Architecture Components

### 1. BottomNav (Main Component)
**File:** `BottomNav.tsx`

The main orchestrator component that renders different bottom navbar variants.

```tsx
import { BottomNav } from '@/components/BottomContainer/BottomNav';

<BottomNav 
    variant="search-certificate"
    onBack={() => navigate(-1)}
    className="custom-styles"
    isFixed={true}
/>
```

**Props:**
- `variant` - Type of bottom nav to render (e.g., "search-certificate", "search-notification")
- `onBack` - Optional callback for back button functionality
- `className` - Optional custom styling classes
- `isFixed` - Whether to use fixed width (343px) or full width

### 2. BottomContainerContext (Context Provider)
**File:** `context.tsx`

Provides shared state and callbacks to all bottom navbar variants.

```tsx
interface BottomContainerContextType {
    children?: React.ReactNode;
    className?: ClassValue;
    onBack?: () => void;
}
```

**Usage in variants:**
```tsx
import { useBottomContainerContext } from './context';

export const SearchCertificateNav = () => {
    const { onBack, className } = useBottomContainerContext();
    
    return (
        <div className={cn(className, "custom-styles")}>
            <button onClick={onBack}>Back</button>
        </div>
    );
};
```

### 3. Zustand Stores (State Management)
**File:** `stores.ts`

Feature-specific state management using Zustand.

```tsx
import { create } from "zustand";

interface SearchCertificateNavStore {
    searchQuery: string;
    setSearchQuery: (searchQuery: string) => void;
}

export const useSearchCertificateNavStore = create<SearchCertificateNavStore>((set) => ({
    searchQuery: "",
    setSearchQuery: (searchQuery: string) => set({ searchQuery }),
}));
```

### 4. Variant Components
**Example:** `SearchCertificateNav.tsx`

Individual bottom navbar implementations for specific features.

```tsx
import { useBottomContainerContext } from "./context";
import { useSearchCertificateNavStore } from "./stores";
import { useTranslation } from "react-i18next";
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

export const SearchCertificateNav = () => {
    const { searchQuery, setSearchQuery } = useSearchCertificateNavStore();
    const { onBack, className } = useBottomContainerContext();
    const { t } = useTranslation();

    return (
        <div className={cn(className, "flex items-center gap-1.5 h-13 bg-primary rounded-xl p-1.5")}>
            <button onClick={onBack}>Back</button>
            <input
                type="text"
                value={searchQuery}
                onChange={(e) => setSearchQuery(e.target.value)}
                placeholder={t("participant.certificates.searchPlaceholder")}
            />
        </div>
    );
};
```

## Creating a New Bottom Nav Variant

### Step 1: Create the Zustand Store (if needed)

Add to `stores.ts`:
```tsx
interface MyFeatureNavStore {
    myState: string;
    setMyState: (value: string) => void;
}

export const useMyFeatureNavStore = create<MyFeatureNavStore>((set) => ({
    myState: "",
    setMyState: (value: string) => set({ myState: value }),
}));
```

### Step 2: Create the Variant Component

Create `MyFeatureNav.tsx`:
```tsx
import { useBottomContainerContext } from "./context";
import { useMyFeatureNavStore } from "./stores";
import { useTranslation } from "react-i18next";
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

export const MyFeatureNav = () => {
    const { myState, setMyState } = useMyFeatureNavStore();
    const { onBack, className } = useBottomContainerContext();
    const { t } = useTranslation();

    return (
        <div className={cn(className, "flex items-center gap-2 bg-background p-3")}>
            {/* Your UI here */}
        </div>
    );
};
```

### Step 3: Register in BottomNav

Update `BottomNav.tsx`:
```tsx
import { MyFeatureNav } from "./MyFeatureNav";

type BottomNavVariant = "search-certificate" | "search-notification" | "my-feature";

const content = useMemo(() => {
    switch (variant) {
        case "search-certificate":
            return <SearchCertificateNav />;
        case "search-notification":
            return <SearchNotificationNav />;
        case "my-feature":
            return <MyFeatureNav />;
        default:
            return null;
    }
}, [variant]);
```

### Step 4: Add i18n Translations

Add to `apps/web/src/lib/i18n/locales/en.json`:
```json
{
    "myFeature": {
        "nav": {
            "placeholder": "Search...",
            "button": "Action"
        }
    }
}
```

And `th.json`:
```json
{
    "myFeature": {
        "nav": {
            "placeholder": "ค้นหา...",
            "button": "ดำเนินการ"
        }
    }
}
```

## Usage in Pages

### Example: Certificate List Page

```tsx
import { BottomNav } from '@/components/BottomContainer/BottomNav';
import { useNavigate } from 'react-router-dom';

export const CertificatesPage = () => {
    const navigate = useNavigate();

    return (
        <div>
            {/* Page content */}
            <BottomNav 
                variant="search-certificate"
                onBack={() => navigate(-1)}
                isFixed={false}
            />
        </div>
    );
};
```

## Accessing State in Page Components

Zustand stores can be accessed from any component:

```tsx
import { useSearchCertificateNavStore } from '@/components/BottomContainer/stores';

export const CertificateList = () => {
    const { searchQuery } = useSearchCertificateNavStore();
    
    const filteredCertificates = certificates.filter(cert =>
        cert.name.toLowerCase().includes(searchQuery.toLowerCase())
    );

    return (
        <div>
            {filteredCertificates.map(cert => (
                <CertificateCard key={cert.id} certificate={cert} />
            ))}
        </div>
    );
};
```

